Urgency: medium
Maintainer: fehlix <fehlix@mxlinux.org>
Changed-By: fehlix <fehlix@mxlinux.org>
Description: 
 live-busybox - static BusyBox binary for the MX/antiX live-initrd
Changes:
 live-busybox (1.38.0-3mx1) mx; urgency=medium
 .
   * New package: static busybox for the MX/antiX live-initrd, built from
     Debian's busybox 1:1.38.0-3 source (incl. all Debian patches).
   * Single flavour "live", config debian/config/pkg/live, derived from the
     config embedded in the previously used BusyBox v1.31.1 (bbconfig),
     updated to 1.38.0 with oldconfig:
     - same applet set as before (new 1.38 applets disabled)
     - static build; use busybox own passwd/group handling and crypt
       (incl. yescrypt), as Debian's busybox-static does
   * Link statically against musl instead of glibc (616K instead of 1.7M):
     - FEATURE_VI_REGEX_SEARCH disabled (needs GNU regex, not in musl)
     - debian/testsuite-musl.diff: skip 2 tests failing due to musl limits
       (awk "\<" with empty match, needs REG_STARTEND; date -d with a
       timezone in the date string, needs strptime %z)
   * debian/patches/live-ttyname-fallback-without-proc.patch:
     xmalloc_ttyname() falls back to scanning /dev when /proc is not
     mounted (musl ttyname_r needs /proc/self/fd); fixes "tty" printing
     "not a tty" in the early initrd (init: setfont $file -C $(tty)).
   * Installs into /usr/lib/live-busybox/ only, no applet symlinks.
